WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.630
Between 2002 and 2008, satellites measured
the groundwater beneath north-west

2
00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:10.030
India falling by 109 cubic kilometres.

3
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.990
That's double the capacity of
India's largest surface reservoir,

4
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.930
while rainfall was close to normal.

5
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.870
Food has hidden costs.

6
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:24.670
On global average, a kilogram of beef
has a water footprint of 15,400 litres.

7
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.750
Of every 100 calories the
world's crops produce,

8
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.130
how many reach people
as meat, milk or eggs?

9
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.230
About 50?

10
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.170
70?

11
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:37.790
In this mission, you'll model
food production as a system,

12
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.030
tracing energy and water.

13
00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.290
Then you'll compare water footprints,
and judge which foods and places are more

14
00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.710
sustainable.

15
00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:50.630
Your mission: calculate how many of
every 100 calories from the world's crops

16
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:53.550
reach people as meat, milk or eggs.
